1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,669
In the fall of 2017, teams of federal agents

2
00:00:04,669 --> 00:00:07,421
fan out across the United States.

3
00:00:07,871 --> 00:00:11,754
Over five weeks, they arrest 214 people in

4
00:00:11,754 --> 00:00:13,233
American cities.

5
00:00:13,233 --> 00:00:16,746
In El Salvador, police arrest 53 more.

6
00:00:17,196 --> 00:00:20,609
267 arrests. One target.

7
00:00:21,059 --> 00:00:24,179
The gang they're hunting wasn't born in a

8
00:00:24,179 --> 00:00:25,853
jungle, or a war zone.

9
00:00:25,853 --> 00:00:27,907
It was born in Los Angeles.

10
00:00:28,357 --> 00:00:31,425
And for 40 years, crackdown after crackdown

11
00:00:31,425 --> 00:00:33,279
has failed to wipe it out.

12
00:00:33,279 --> 00:00:35,205
Some only made it stronger.

13
00:00:41,008 --> 00:00:45,253
To understand MS-13, you have to start with a war.

14
00:00:45,703 --> 00:00:49,840
From 1979 to 1992, El Salvador is torn apart

15
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:51,062
by civil war.

16
00:00:51,062 --> 00:00:53,977
Leftist guerrillas on one side.

17
00:00:53,977 --> 00:00:58,866
The army, and government death squads, on the other.

18
00:00:59,316 --> 00:01:02,758
An estimated 75,000 people are killed.

19
00:01:02,758 --> 00:01:04,841
Most of them civilians.

20
00:01:05,291 --> 00:01:08,825
Hundreds of thousands of Salvadorans flee north.

21
00:01:08,825 --> 00:01:12,579
More of them settle in one city than anywhere else.

22
00:01:12,579 --> 00:01:13,462
Los Angeles.

23
00:01:13,912 --> 00:01:17,732
They crowd into neighborhoods just west of downtown.

24
00:01:17,732 --> 00:01:19,275
Pico-Union. Westlake.

25
00:01:19,275 --> 00:01:22,140
Cheap apartments, packed buildings, and

26
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:25,005
streets already claimed by older gangs.

27
00:01:25,455 --> 00:01:28,640
For the new arrivals, many of them teenagers,

28
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:30,622
those streets are dangerous.

29
00:01:30,622 --> 00:01:33,029
The established gangs target them.

30
00:01:33,479 --> 00:01:36,315
So by the early 1980s, a group of young

31
00:01:36,315 --> 00:01:39,516
Salvadorans has started a gang of their own.

32
00:01:39,966 --> 00:01:41,332
At first it's loose.

33
00:01:41,332 --> 00:01:43,996
Kids who love heavy metal, who hang out

34
00:01:43,996 --> 00:01:46,591
together and watch each other's backs.

35
00:01:46,591 --> 00:01:49,459
They call themselves the Mara Salvatrucha.

36
00:01:49,909 --> 00:01:53,331
Mara is Central American slang for a gang.

37
00:01:53,331 --> 00:01:57,324
It may come from marabunta, a swarm of army ants.

38
00:01:57,324 --> 00:02:00,746
Salvatrucha blends Salvadoran with trucha,

39
00:02:00,746 --> 00:02:03,435
street slang for sharp, or alert.

40
00:02:03,885 --> 00:02:06,847
Some of the members have seen the war up close.

41
00:02:06,847 --> 00:02:08,360
A few have fought in it.

42
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:10,818
And that changes what the gang becomes.

43
00:02:11,268 --> 00:02:14,384
One early leader is a former Salvadoran

44
00:02:14,384 --> 00:02:17,739
soldier with elite, U.S.-advised training.

45
00:02:17,739 --> 00:02:21,175
By the early 1990s, he's running his clique

46
00:02:21,175 --> 00:02:23,172
with military discipline.

47
00:02:23,622 --> 00:02:26,609
As the gang grows, it lines up with the

48
00:02:26,609 --> 00:02:29,901
Sureños, the Southern California gangs that

49
00:02:29,901 --> 00:02:33,347
answer to the Mexican Mafia inside the prison

50
00:02:33,347 --> 00:02:33,883
system.

51
00:02:34,333 --> 00:02:37,997
That alliance is believed to give the gang its

52
00:02:37,997 --> 00:02:39,352
number. Thirteen.

53
00:02:39,352 --> 00:02:42,936
For M, the thirteenth letter of the alphabet.

54
00:02:42,936 --> 00:02:45,405
Mara Salvatrucha becomes MS-13.

55
00:02:46,405 --> 00:02:49,554
In 1992, the war in El Salvador ends.

56
00:02:49,554 --> 00:02:53,043
And the United States starts sending gang

57
00:02:53,043 --> 00:02:54,149
members back.

58
00:02:54,599 --> 00:02:57,740
Through the 1990s, Washington steps up

59
00:02:57,740 --> 00:03:01,790
deportations of non-citizens convicted of crimes.

60
00:03:01,790 --> 00:03:05,344
Young men with Los Angeles gang tattoos are

61
00:03:05,344 --> 00:03:09,146
put on planes to San Salvador, Tegucigalpa and

62
00:03:09,146 --> 00:03:10,386
Guatemala City.

63
00:03:10,836 --> 00:03:14,001
Many of them barely remember those countries.

64
00:03:14,001 --> 00:03:15,830
Some hardly speak Spanish.

65
00:03:15,830 --> 00:03:17,940
What they do know is the gang.

66
00:03:18,390 --> 00:03:21,564
El Salvador has just come out of twelve years

67
00:03:21,564 --> 00:03:22,057
of war.

68
00:03:22,057 --> 00:03:25,160
Its new national police force is being built

69
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:26,077
from scratch.

70
00:03:26,077 --> 00:03:29,462
There are weapons everywhere, and very few jobs.

71
00:03:29,912 --> 00:03:33,539
For MS-13, it's the perfect place to grow.

72
00:03:33,989 --> 00:03:36,595
Deported members start new cliques.

73
00:03:36,595 --> 00:03:38,382
They recruit local kids.

74
00:03:38,382 --> 00:03:41,286
And a gang that began as protection for

75
00:03:41,286 --> 00:03:44,339
refugees in Los Angeles takes root across

76
00:03:44,339 --> 00:03:45,530
Central America.

77
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:47,775
Then the flow reverses.

78
00:03:47,775 --> 00:03:49,727
New members travel north.

79
00:03:49,727 --> 00:03:53,786
The gang spreads across the United States. Virginia.

80
00:03:53,786 --> 00:03:56,049
Maryland. Texas. Long Island.

81
00:03:56,499 --> 00:03:59,337
Some deported members simply came back.

82
00:03:59,337 --> 00:04:00,574
Again, and again.

83
00:04:01,024 --> 00:04:04,601
By 2009, the FBI estimates 8,000 to 10,000

84
00:04:04,601 --> 00:04:08,092
members in the United States, and tens of

85
00:04:08,092 --> 00:04:11,328
thousands more across Central America.

86
00:04:12,328 --> 00:04:14,256
MS-13 is not a cartel.

87
00:04:14,256 --> 00:04:18,200
It doesn't have one boss at the top of a drug

88
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:18,813
empire.

89
00:04:19,263 --> 00:04:20,876
It's built from cliques.

90
00:04:20,876 --> 00:04:23,766
Small neighborhood units, each with its own

91
00:04:23,766 --> 00:04:26,858
leaders, its own territory and its own crimes.

92
00:04:27,308 --> 00:04:29,630
Its core business is extortion.

93
00:04:29,630 --> 00:04:32,927
In El Salvador, bus drivers, shop owners and

94
00:04:32,927 --> 00:04:36,073
street vendors pay rent to the gang, often

95
00:04:36,073 --> 00:04:36,897
every week.

96
00:04:36,897 --> 00:04:40,044
Those who refuse are threatened, or worse.

97
00:04:40,494 --> 00:04:43,731
Above the cliques sits a council of senior

98
00:04:43,731 --> 00:04:47,430
leaders, most of them inside Salvadoran prisons.

99
00:04:47,430 --> 00:04:50,513
Prosecutors call it the Ranfla Nacional.

100
00:04:50,513 --> 00:04:52,825
The gang's board of directors.

101
00:04:53,275 --> 00:04:56,797
And its trademark is violence meant to be seen.

102
00:04:56,797 --> 00:05:00,020
Attacks often carried out with machetes and

103
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:01,669
knives, not just guns.

104
00:05:01,669 --> 00:05:04,667
Not only to kill, but to send a message.

105
00:05:05,667 --> 00:05:08,184
The United States answers with a hunt.

106
00:05:08,634 --> 00:05:13,236
In 2004, the FBI creates a national task force

107
00:05:13,236 --> 00:05:17,338
dedicated to a single street gang. MS-13.

108
00:05:17,788 --> 00:05:20,029
In October 2012, the U.S.

109
00:05:20,029 --> 00:05:22,001
Treasury goes further.

110
00:05:22,001 --> 00:05:25,944
It designates MS-13 a transnational criminal

111
00:05:25,944 --> 00:05:27,109
organization.

112
00:05:27,109 --> 00:05:31,143
The first street gang ever to get that label.

113
00:05:31,593 --> 00:05:34,838
The designation lets investigators go after

114
00:05:34,838 --> 00:05:35,593
the money.

115
00:05:35,593 --> 00:05:38,838
The head of immigration enforcement says it

116
00:05:38,838 --> 00:05:42,537
lets them strike at the financial heart of MS-13.

117
00:05:42,987 --> 00:05:46,792
Homeland Security Investigations launches wave

118
00:05:46,792 --> 00:05:49,853
after wave of nationwide gang surges.

119
00:05:49,853 --> 00:05:53,824
Raids in dozens of cities, often before sunrise.

120
00:05:54,274 --> 00:05:57,354
But on Long Island, east of New York City, the

121
00:05:57,354 --> 00:05:59,095
violence is getting worse.

122
00:05:59,545 --> 00:06:03,523
In 2016 and 2017, a wave of killings of

123
00:06:03,523 --> 00:06:07,807
teenagers and young men stuns the suburbs.

124
00:06:07,807 --> 00:06:12,601
Investigators link them to local MS-13 cliques.

125
00:06:13,051 --> 00:06:16,817
In April 2017, four young men are lured into a

126
00:06:16,817 --> 00:06:19,682
park in Central Islip and murdered.

127
00:06:19,682 --> 00:06:23,611
One of the attackers was just fifteen years old.

128
00:06:24,061 --> 00:06:27,388
Those cases put MS-13 on front pages across

129
00:06:27,388 --> 00:06:28,316
the country.

130
00:06:28,316 --> 00:06:31,256
And they set the stage for the biggest

131
00:06:31,256 --> 00:06:32,339
crackdown yet.

132
00:06:32,789 --> 00:06:34,857
Operation Raging Bull.

133
00:06:34,857 --> 00:06:38,523
Phase one runs in El Salvador, after an

134
00:06:38,523 --> 00:06:41,813
18-month investigation. 53 arrests.

135
00:06:42,263 --> 00:06:47,359
Phase two hits American cities between October

136
00:06:47,359 --> 00:06:51,457
8 and November 11, 2017. 214 arrests.

137
00:06:51,907 --> 00:06:56,203
93 of them face criminal charges, ranging from

138
00:06:56,203 --> 00:06:58,724
illegal re-entry to murder.

139
00:06:58,724 --> 00:07:03,299
The other 121 are held on immigration violations.

140
00:07:03,749 --> 00:07:06,666
The acting director of ICE sums it up.

141
00:07:06,666 --> 00:07:10,427
“This is a great operation, but we are not done.”

142
00:07:11,427 --> 00:07:14,387
Arresting foot soldiers isn't enough.

143
00:07:14,387 --> 00:07:17,987
In 2019, the Justice Department creates Joint

144
00:07:17,987 --> 00:07:21,987
Task Force Vulcan, aimed at the leadership itself.

145
00:07:22,437 --> 00:07:25,850
In January 2021, prosecutors in New York

146
00:07:25,850 --> 00:07:29,605
unseal an indictment against fourteen of the

147
00:07:29,605 --> 00:07:32,250
gang's highest-ranking leaders.

148
00:07:32,250 --> 00:07:33,957
The Ranfla Nacional.

149
00:07:34,407 --> 00:07:36,823
The charges include terrorism.

150
00:07:36,823 --> 00:07:40,125
Conspiracy to provide material support to

151
00:07:40,125 --> 00:07:41,011
terrorists.

152
00:07:41,011 --> 00:07:42,300
Narco-terrorism.

153
00:07:42,750 --> 00:07:46,179
Prosecutors allege that from around 2012 to

154
00:07:46,179 --> 00:07:49,687
2015, the gang's leaders struck a truce with

155
00:07:49,687 --> 00:07:52,478
the then-government of El Salvador.

156
00:07:52,478 --> 00:07:55,987
Fewer murders, in exchange for better prison

157
00:07:55,987 --> 00:07:59,177
conditions, benefits, and cash payments.

158
00:07:59,627 --> 00:08:02,662
The Justice Department calls it the most

159
00:08:02,662 --> 00:08:06,229
sweeping indictment ever brought against MS-13.

160
00:08:06,229 --> 00:08:09,568
The charges remain allegations unless proven

161
00:08:09,568 --> 00:08:10,251
in court.

162
00:08:10,701 --> 00:08:14,470
And in February 2025, the State Department

163
00:08:14,470 --> 00:08:18,508
formally designates MS-13 a Foreign Terrorist

164
00:08:18,508 --> 00:08:19,675
Organization.

165
00:08:19,675 --> 00:08:23,534
A street gang from Los Angeles, on the same

166
00:08:23,534 --> 00:08:26,765
list as international terror groups.

167
00:08:27,765 --> 00:08:30,905
In El Salvador, the turning point comes on a

168
00:08:30,905 --> 00:08:31,690
single day.

169
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:33,629
March 26, 2022.

170
00:08:33,629 --> 00:08:35,714
62 people are killed.

171
00:08:35,714 --> 00:08:40,082
The most violent day the country has seen in

172
00:08:40,082 --> 00:08:42,167
nearly three decades.

173
00:08:42,617 --> 00:08:45,849
The next day, El Salvador declares a state of

174
00:08:45,849 --> 00:08:48,793
exception, suspending some constitutional

175
00:08:48,793 --> 00:08:49,655
protections.

176
00:08:49,655 --> 00:08:52,384
Soldiers and police sweep through gang

177
00:08:52,384 --> 00:08:53,390
neighborhoods.

178
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:57,835
By the end of 2024, more than 83,000 people

179
00:08:57,835 --> 00:08:59,600
have been arrested.

180
00:09:00,050 --> 00:09:03,407
In early 2023, the government opens a

181
00:09:03,407 --> 00:09:06,763
mega-prison built for 40,000 inmates.

182
00:09:06,763 --> 00:09:09,757
The Terrorism Confinement Center.

183
00:09:10,207 --> 00:09:13,417
According to the government, homicides fall to

184
00:09:13,417 --> 00:09:14,394
historic lows.

185
00:09:14,394 --> 00:09:17,464
Many Salvadorans say they can walk their own

186
00:09:17,464 --> 00:09:18,441
streets again.

187
00:09:18,891 --> 00:09:22,222
But human rights groups warn of mass arrests

188
00:09:22,222 --> 00:09:23,736
without due process.

189
00:09:23,736 --> 00:09:27,218
President Bukele says around 8,000 people have

190
00:09:27,218 --> 00:09:28,278
been released.

191
00:09:28,278 --> 00:09:31,533
Rights groups say many more innocent people

192
00:09:31,533 --> 00:09:32,971
remain behind bars.

193
00:09:33,421 --> 00:09:37,589
And in March 2025, the story comes full circle.

194
00:09:37,589 --> 00:09:41,667
The United States sends about 250 deportees to

195
00:09:41,667 --> 00:09:45,037
that prison, most of them Venezuelans,

196
00:09:45,037 --> 00:09:48,140
including 23 alleged MS-13 members.

197
00:09:48,140 --> 00:09:52,041
The transfers are still being fought over in

198
00:09:52,041 --> 00:09:53,283
federal court.

199
00:09:54,483 --> 00:09:58,124
40 years ago, MS-13 was a group of refugee

200
00:09:58,124 --> 00:10:01,938
kids trying to survive on the streets of Los

201
00:10:01,938 --> 00:10:02,632
Angeles.

202
00:10:03,082 --> 00:10:05,903
Since then it has been called a criminal

203
00:10:05,903 --> 00:10:08,935
organization, a terrorist organization, and

204
00:10:08,935 --> 00:10:11,615
the target of some of the biggest gang

205
00:10:11,615 --> 00:10:12,955
crackdowns the U.S.

206
00:10:12,955 --> 00:10:14,154
has ever mounted.

207
00:10:14,604 --> 00:10:16,530
Every crackdown changed it.

208
00:10:16,530 --> 00:10:18,171
Deportations spread it.

209
00:10:18,171 --> 00:10:19,670
Prisons organized it.

210
00:10:19,670 --> 00:10:21,025
Raids scattered it.

211
00:10:21,475 --> 00:10:24,283
Whether this crackdown finally ends it is a

212
00:10:24,283 --> 00:10:25,785
case that's still open.
